  <constraints>
    <constraint source="task-202 punch list verification obligation">Executor MUST grep-verify each row's actual code state BEFORE applying to prevent double-fixing. Wave G-7/G-8 batches (tasks ~155-198+) landed many fixes; verification matrix already found 8 of 22 rows `already-applied`. Same discipline here — no code changes without verification evidence + row annotation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10 BFF hygiene">Any change to src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ or src/server/shared/Spaarke.*/ MUST report publish-size + delta in PR per CLAUDE.md §10; ceiling ≤60 MB compressed; current baseline 44.96 MB incl. PDBs (2026-08-13 net10 framework-dependent linux-x64). Threshold for escalation: ≥+5 MB single-task delta requires explicit justification.</constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md § F test update obligation">Rows B14 (Infrastructure/Auth) + B18 (EnvVarValuesOptions refactor) + B22 (AI endpoints) MUST have accompanying unit/integration test additions/updates per `bff-extensions.md` § F. Exceptions require code review sign-off with reason.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032 asymmetric-registration governance">If B18 refactor touches DI registration inside `if (flag)` blocks, apply ADR-032 F.1 static-scan recipe + Null-Object kill-switch pattern (P1/P2/P3) per `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` § F.1.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §11 Component Justification">All 6 rows are MODIFICATION-only (edit existing files); §11 does NOT trigger. If verification surfaces a row that would require a NEW component, escalate rather than expanding scope silently.</constraint>
  </constraints>

