  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL, sonnet/high). Read `notes/task-202-punch-list.md` Class-B verification matrix in full. Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` (mandatory before BFF touch). Read `.claude/constraints/testing.md`.</step>
    <step order="1" name="B10 verify H6/H7 credential config">Grep for `SolutionImportOptions.ClientSecret` + `EnvVarValuesOptions.ClientSecret` KV binding provisioning in `customer.bicep` + `kv-secrets.generated.bicep`. If KV binding provisioned + consumed → annotate `already-applied`. If OPEN → provision KV binding + wire consumer path + row-level test (~4h).</step>
    <step order="2" name="B14 verify ManagedIdentityCredentialFactory">Read `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Auth/ManagedIdentityCredentialFactory.cs` end-to-end. Determine whether TenantId-scope gap (per `GraphClientFactory` analogue) exists — options-level TenantId source vs per-call scope. If gap real → extend I5 ArchTest (`Spaarke.ArchTests.TenantIsolation.I5_*`) to cover `Infrastructure/Auth` (currently scoped to `Infrastructure/Graph`) + fix the factory + tests (~3h). If no gap → annotate `not-applicable`.</step>
    <step order="3" name="B16 verify H2b retired-lineage reject">Read `H2bAiSearchIndexHandler` + `CanonicalIndexCatalog`. Grep for the full retired lineage list (not just `spaarke-playbook-embeddings` but also historic aliases per `ai-search-catalog-audit`). If reject covers only `spaarke-playbook-embeddings` → extend to full retired lineage + tests (~2h). If already comprehensive → annotate `already-applied`.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Checkpoint">Run context-handoff (silent "✅ Checkpoint.") — 3 rows complete, 3 remaining.</step>
    <step order="5" name="B18 verify EnvVarValuesOptions refactor">Grep for `KeyVaultSecretRef` seam landed by task 084 in shared options. If seam landed AND `EnvVarValuesOptions.ClientSecret` still cleartext → refactor to `KeyVaultSecretRef` per shared pattern + tests + verify no HIGH-severity CVE from `dotnet list package --vulnerable` (~6h). If task 084 seam not landed → annotate `blocked-on-084`. If already refactored → annotate `already-applied`.</step>
    <step order="6" name="B20 verify Worker Program.cs comment drift">Read `src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Worker/Program.cs:784-795` verbatim. If comments still claim placeholders in use (contradicting Wave G-6/G-7 real-impl landings) → correct comment to reflect current registration state + explain retirement (~1h). If comments already accurate → annotate `already-applied`.</step>
    <step order="7" name="B22 verify 429 wireup at AI endpoints">Grep `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/**/*.cs` for `Results.Problem` / `429` / `TooManyRequests` at each of ~30 AI-consuming endpoints (task 077 deferred list). Enumerate current wire-up state. If task 077 deferred wire-up still pending → wire per endpoint + tests + verify publish-size delta (~8h — largest of the 6 rows). If landed → annotate `already-applied`.</step>
    <step order="8" name="Annotate verification matrix">For each of 6 rows, update `notes/task-202-punch-list.md` Class-B verification matrix `Verified status` column with one of: `applied 2026-XX-XX task 204a` OR `already-applied — evidence: <cite>` OR `not-applicable — reason: <cite>` OR `blocked-on-XXX`.</step>
    <step order="9" name="Build + publish-size verify">`dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` — 0 warnings 0 errors. If any row shipped BFF code: `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/` — record compressed size + delta vs 44.96 MB baseline in task notes.</step>
    <step order="9.5" name="Quality gates">FULL rigor + BFF/tests touched → invoke `code-review` + `adr-check` skills per root CLAUDE.md §8. Address any Critical findings before marking complete.</step>
    <step order="10" name="Report">Update `current-task.md` + `TASK-INDEX.md`; cross-reference the annotated verification matrix + per-row outcomes; note total effort vs 15-25h estimate (may reduce).</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any row's verification reveals a DIFFERENT bug than the punch-list row's title (e.g., B18's ClientSecret refactor uncovers a broader shared-options structural issue), STOP and file a new punch-list row rather than silently expanding this task's scope. Task 202's punch list is the authority for what's in scope; expansion requires explicit re-scoping.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any row's fix would require touching `.claude/` paths (patterns / constraints / skills), STOP and defer to main session per root CLAUDE.md §3 Sub-Agent Write Boundary. This task's `parallel-safe: true` presumes zero `.claude/` writes.</trigger>
    <trigger>If BFF publish-size delta ≥+5 MB for a single row, escalate per §10 threshold rule with explicit justification. If cumulative ≥55 MB triggers architecture review; ≥60 MB is HARD STOP.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a row's fix reveals an ADR conflict (e.g., B14 I5 ArchTest scope extension challenges an ADR-028 rule), invoke root CLAUDE.md §6.5 ADR Conflict Resolution protocol — do NOT silently comply or violate.</trigger>
  </escalation>

